# Secrets. .env.example is the committed template; a filled-in .env never is.
.env

# Virtual environment and build artifacts
.venv/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Tool caches
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Real-job measurements (scripts/measure_jobs.py). jobs.jsonl carries fetched third-party
# page text and report bodies, and run.log carries every query and URL the tools logged at
# INFO. Only the summary table is published, and it goes into the docs.
measurements/

# Private working documents. Not published: both carry personal interview-preparation
# material rather than project documentation - interview-prep.md maps résumé claims to what
# is actually built (including the claims that must not be made), and the guidelines embed
# the same "say this, do not say that" interview wording alongside the engineering standards.
# The local files stay; they are simply not tracked.
docs/interview-prep.md
docs/engineering-guidelines.md
